    "step": "org A genuine findings",
    "ok": true,
    "detail": [
      "delete_book deletes any book by id without checking the book's owner, so one user's book can be removed by another authenticated user (may not be enforced in DELETE /books/{book_id}).",
      "get_book returns the owner's notes for any book id without an ownership check, so one user may read another user's private notes (may not be enforced in GET /books/{book_id}).",
      "delete_book has no role check, so any authenticated caller (including a read-only role) can delete books (may not be enforced in DELETE /books/{book_id}).",
      "Deleted seed book is resurrected on the next request",
      "Documented SQL injection in get_book is not reachable through the route",
      "Oversized integer book id causes a server error (refuted)",
      "[unclassified] Forgeable bearer token: any 'Bearer demo-<anything>' is accepted and the suffix becomes the user identity (documented flaw 1)",
      "[CWE-862] Mutating DELETE route has no authorization or ownership check (documented flaw 5)"
    ]
  },
